  "query_preview": ".. /Saturday through Wednesday/... The low pressure \nsystem and associated front will continue moving Southeast through\nthe Alaska Panhandle Saturday. Overall, the weather pattern for \nSaturday looks less favorable aloft for thunderstorms, but there \ncould be some convective shower activity moving into Southeast \nAlaska from British Columbia. \n\nA low pressure system in the Gulf of Alaska may bring some stronger \nwinds (up to 15 kts) and higher rain chances Monday into the\nmiddle of next week. Right now, the low looks to be fairly \ndisorganized, but the strongest winds (up to 20 kts) are forecast\nto be near Cape Suckling, as the GFS hints at a barrier jet \nformation. As of now, confidence in this occurring is low, but it \nis a possibility to monitor.",
